{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice","id":1083900,"title":"I want to try and commit Diablerie for the first time. Looking for advice.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-26T02:25:19-07:00","id":1083900,"title":"I want to try and commit Diablerie for the first time. Looking for advice.","content":"So, as the title says, I'm looking for some help in pulling of a successful Diablerie. I've been playing VtM and VtR (mostly the latter these days.) for gods damned AGES, and I've literally never even seen a Diablerie attempted, let alone pulled off. It's just never come up in the various groups I've been in, although I suspect a large portion of that is due to extreme luck in avoiding &quot;that guy&quot; in my gaming group, at least for NWoD games. So, with that little disclaimer out of the way, I was wondering if you might be willing to help me try and commit and get away with my first Diablerie ever. I've spoken with my ST, and they're okay with it, and even went to the trouble of clarifying that, to their mind, the Tainted condition is what Auspex picks up, not just the act of Diablerie itself. So once that goes away, no more auspex outings at level 2. Level 4 might still do it, depending on the circumstances though.<br /> <br /> Enough of the preliminaries though. Here's the slightly more relevant details for the act itself. I want to diablerize my sire, a woman named Anabelle in the Ordo Dracul, a minority and out of power faction within the city of Paris, France in 1999. I am also a member of the Ordo. My sire is a Nosferatu, Mystery of the Ascendant, and I am a Nosferatu, Mystery of the Wyrm. I only have the first dot. I am currently blood-bonded to my sire at the third level, which is both illegal in the city, and the reason my character wants her deader than dead. This is the third time in his life this has happened. First when he was mortal, then when he was a ghoul, and finally, lastly, as a kindred. I do understand he has some intense and loving devotion towards her, but he's built up enough simultaneous hatred in his heart over the years I think it could be plausible. The ST seems inclined to agree at least. Other than that, I have Blood Potency 2, 2 dots in Brawl and 3 in Strength, and 2 in Vigor. My sire, Anabelle is very much a non-combatant, although I'm sure it'd be a hell of a mess if it came to straight fisticuffs just due to power disparities, but not unwinnable. She tends to harbor guests and students (me) in a small apartment/library and only has a single ghoul retainer on hand at most times. She has a single other student, another player, who is currently distracting or otherwise inhibiting the ghoul as part of their personal activities. The city itself is Carthian run, abhors the act of Diablerie, but has also declared any form of Viniculum to be illegal as it is tantamount to slavery. This only applies to Kindred though.<br /> <br /> That's all I can think of for relevant details, at the moment. Please, feel free to ask questions about the situation or my character or whatever you feel is pertinent and relevant. I hope that crowd-sourcing this question and idea to a larger audience, and a more experienced one with this particular subject might give me a greater chance of actually pulling off something that I've never really had the chance to see in game, and would very much like to explore. Thank you for any and all responses. I eagerly await them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T03:51:49-07:00","id":1083907,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify - Did your ST say Auspex 2 only detects diablerie if your character has the tainted condition active? (That's how I run it personally.) If the answer to this is yes, my response is going to be based on that answer and what your &quot;character&quot; knows in regards to diablerie.<br /> Is your character actually aware of the tainted condition and the specifics. (If your ST allows, your character can potentally pawn off self experimentation with that to develop a scale that conceals the condition and advance in the Ordo as well. Or an Obfuscate only devotion to conceal specific details from being uncovered.)<br /> How legalistic and forgiving are the Carthian courts for the crime of diablerie? Patricide? Killing in &quot;self defense&quot;? Your character should be prepared for the possibility that they'll be discovered and that they'll have multiple infallible lie detection and truth extraction methods via Auspex, Invictus Oaths, Carthian Law, Cruac, and Theban Sorcery. So a credible explanation of extenuating circumstances may be needed. Your character may be able to mount a self defense case stemming from allegations that your character's sire forced your character under vinculum and experimented on him.<br /> Do they count crimes committed outside the domain as &quot;prosecutable&quot; or is it deemed outside their jurisdiction? (I played in an Invictus domain setting like that, where it was a favorite Carthian and Crone tactic to drag rivals outside the city borders and torpor or kill them. Until it started backfiring. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> Does your character's sire have any other childer or family in the domain. What about other Nosferatu in the city? (Again. This sort of falls under information your character may or may not know about.)<br /> I would advise disposing of her ghoul. (He could be a possible witness against you via manufactured blood sympathy.) Or may seek revenge until the vinculum wears off.<br /> Another option is to skip town or go into torpor for a few months until the tainted condition is resolved and claim &quot;educational pursuits&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T05:27:43-07:00","id":1083924,"title":"","content":"A few caveats. First, blood bonds expire when the bonding party dies. You don't need to diablerize your sire to destroy the blood bond. If you really feel the need to get the bond out of the way prior to her death, you could possibly owe someone within the Order of the voivode mystery a boon and have them use the blood cleansing ritual on you. It's a fairly basic scale that involves rolling your blood potency against that of the bonding party though it's possible to artificially boost it by spending more vitae on the scale. However, if your goal is diablerie because of a personal vendetta, I would advise caution due to some fairly obvious things like addiction to vitae, addiction to diablerie, etc.<br /> <br /> All that aside, you'll want to prepare a defense for your character. Best case scenario, this will be a wholly legitimate one that outlines your sire's crimes in excruciating detail. No well-informed individual ever said however, that kindred were honest creatures. Concocting, &quot;Evidence&quot; is always a way to go if you need to get off scot-free yourself. The middle-ground of course, is always maneuvering your sire into positions where she looks like she's doing something terrible but actually wasn't. Advice on doing that, make sure whatever you've manipulated her into is not technically punishable but seriously frowned on nevertheless. That would provide a false source of frustration and a motive for your character to diablerize her, and ultimately give you a more sympathetic outlook in the crime itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T06:57:05-07:00","id":1083946,"title":"","content":"Nothing in 2nd edition says blood bonds expire at the death of the regnant. That was first edition. 2nd edition, it's left up to the ST to decide if they break upon the regnant's death or if the thrall maintains a semblance of grief or desire for revenge or wishes to continue pursuing what they believe their regnant wanted them to do. The original poster already said their ST concurs that the regnant's mistreatment would constitute sufficent justification to override the vinculum for the PC to diablerize them so it's a needless and unnecessary distraction to go chasing someone down and selling themself into slavery to get the vinculum removed since it doesn't inhibit the act of diablerie in the slightest. The character only takes a hit to their Humanity roll which is likely to fail anyway. The point is that the player wants to act out a diablerie and the consequences. <br /> Also, scales aren't proprietary. &quot;Anyone&quot; can learn them. (Assuming they want to jeopardize their Humanity.) You just get a price break if you know the respective mystery. Of course if said character learned such a scale and offered to perform it as a city service, it could be another avenue to pursue which might also increase the covenant's standing in the city. But that's tangential to the original question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T07:19:46-07:00","id":1083957,"title":"","content":"Save up your Willpower, it was an embarrassing night when one of our diablerists failed the roll to commit it and couldn't go anymore because she used up all her Willpower in the fight to get to that point . You might try to organize something to disable the sire to begin with, a cell of hunters or other enemies to stake her for instance.<br /> <br /> Also be prepared to do something for the addictions. If you're part of a coterie you may not be 'that guy' but with an urge to commit diablerie on all the others, you might become one. And lastly make sure it's worth it. If the targets Blood Potency is low enough and they won't offer any nice Disciplines or useful Skills, you're effectively just blasting away your Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:48:47-07:00","id":1084086,"title":"","content":"I personally hate the &quot;only detected as long as you have Tainted&quot; interpretation. Here is why, and relevant to your question:<br /> <br /> It goes away in months = Blood Potency, minus one month for each Aggravated damage you take.<br /> <br /> Simply give yourself agg damage (Fire is probably the easiest to obtain, and you're Wyrm so you can probably handle the frenzy checks) equal to your Sire's Blood Potency, and you can't ever be detected.<br /> <br /> Just be sure to do it somewhere hidden; aggravated damage is the only kind that actually leaves permanent scars on Kindred.<br /> <br /> This all assumes you know you can &quot;burn&quot; out the taint, but given this seems premeditated and you're Ordo Dracul, this doesn't seem like information that would be hard to find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T12:04:17-07:00","id":1084092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084086#post1084086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally hate the &quot;only detected as long as you have Tainted&quot; interpretation. Here is why, and relevant to your question:<br /> <br /> It goes away in months = Blood Potency, minus one month for each Aggravated damage you take.<br /> <br /> Simply give yourself agg damage (Fire is probably the easiest to obtain, and you're Wyrm so you can probably handle the frenzy checks) equal to your Sire's Blood Potency, and you can't ever be detected.<br /> <br /> Just be sure to do it somewhere hidden; aggravated damage is the only kind that actually leaves permanent scars on Kindred.<br /> <br /> This all assumes you know you can &quot;burn&quot; out the taint, but given this seems premeditated and you're Ordo Dracul, this doesn't seem like information that would be hard to find.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the opinion here. Me and my storyteller have discussed it and ruled that it is unlikely I would know about burning out the Tainted condition, but could find out, but doing so would be a large risk because it would potentially expose me. It just so happens that we're also introducing Strix into the campaign as an unknown at this point in time, so that's a potential reason to be looking into Diablerie marks and the like later on without as much suspicion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1083907#post1083907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify - Did your ST say Auspex 2 only detects diablerie if your character has the tainted condition active? (That's how I run it personally.) If the answer to this is yes, my response is going to be based on that answer and what your &quot;character&quot; knows in regards to diablerie.<br /> Is your character actually aware of the tainted condition and the specifics. (If your ST allows, your character can potentally pawn off self experimentation with that to develop a scale that conceals the condition and advance in the Ordo as well. Or an Obfuscate only devotion to conceal specific details from being uncovered.)<br /> How legalistic and forgiving are the Carthian courts for the crime of diablerie? Patricide? Killing in &quot;self defense&quot;? Your character should be prepared for the possibility that they'll be discovered and that they'll have multiple infallible lie detection and truth extraction methods via Auspex, Invictus Oaths, Carthian Law, Cruac, and Theban Sorcery. So a credible explanation of extenuating circumstances may be needed. Your character may be able to mount a self defense case stemming from allegations that your character's sire forced your character under vinculum and experimented on him.<br /> Do they count crimes committed outside the domain as &quot;prosecutable&quot; or is it deemed outside their jurisdiction? (I played in an Invictus domain setting like that, where it was a favorite Carthian and Crone tactic to drag rivals outside the city borders and torpor or kill them. Until it started backfiring. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> Does your character's sire have any other childer or family in the domain. What about other Nosferatu in the city? (Again. This sort of falls under information your character may or may not know about.)<br /> I would advise disposing of her ghoul. (He could be a possible witness against you via manufactured blood sympathy.) Or may seek revenge until the vinculum wears off.<br /> Another option is to skip town or go into torpor for a few months until the tainted condition is resolved and claim &quot;educational pursuits&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The ST clarified. Auspex 2 only detects the tainted condition, and that is the only way that auspex 2 specifically can detect Diablerie. There are other methods, but Auspex 2 is only good in the immediate for this one instance. Further, with Strix being a new and unknown feature slowly being added to the game, research into Diablerie stains and markings and the like is unlikely to be nearly so restricted or faux pas in the near future. For now though, I only know that &quot;Diablerie is like eating a soul and digesting it for power, it haunts you for months or sometimes years after, and that anyone with the right skills can find out you did it while you are digesting the soul.&quot; ST's words there. I'll work on a case for myself, just on the chance I get caught. I will also need to ask about the city limits vocation. The Carthians are surprisingly strict on a number of matters in this city, insisting that the right to kill is only the domain of the prince and those the prince grants the right to, Viniculum is illegal, as mentioned, and Diablerie is something I imagine not being okay in any circumstance, but I'd need to look into it. I could see some situations where, if played right, it'd work out as a public demonstration. Self-Defense is a potential out. My sire does not have any other childer or siblings in the immediate area. Some are in nearby countries though. Nosferatu make up about 25% of the cities population, which is a rather large 200 kindred overall. So 50 Nosferatu, about. Another player is incidentally working on the ghoul problem for me due to completely unrelated circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1083924#post1083924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that aside, you'll want to prepare a defense for your character. Best case scenario, this will be a wholly legitimate one that outlines your sire's crimes in excruciating detail. No well-informed individual ever said however, that kindred were honest creatures. Concocting, &quot;Evidence&quot; is always a way to go if you need to get off scot-free yourself. The middle-ground of course, is always maneuvering your sire into positions where she looks like she's doing something terrible but actually wasn't. Advice on doing that, make sure whatever you've manipulated her into is not technically punishable but seriously frowned on nevertheless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give an example of this supposed maneuvering? I approve in principle, but have difficulty imagining it in practice, at least right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:40:37-07:00","id":1084130,"title":"","content":"Be aware that Diablerie is an extra special act of evil on top of murder. Having justification to deal out Final Death and expecting that to save you may well result in a Prince saying, &quot;Your sire's crimes were reprehensible and a disgrace to my city. You had every justification to stake her out where she could greet the dawn. Unfortunately, you ate her soul. As such, thank you for your service to my city, rest assured that your soul is safe.&quot;<br /> <br /> Right before he orders his guards to detain you because he plans to stake you out where you can catch a sunrise.<br /> <br /> You can handle this by either going the extra mile to prep for a diablerie charge or you can try to prep for murder and conceal diablerie but you need to handle it somehow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11422-maskedone","name":"MaskedOne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:13:18-07:00","id":1084145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MaskedOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084130#post1084130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be aware that Diablerie is an extra special act of evil on top of murder. Having justification to deal out Final Death and expecting that to save you may well result in a Prince saying, &quot;Your sire's crimes were reprehensible and a disgrace to my city. You had every justification to stake her out where she could greet the dawn. Unfortunately, you ate her soul. As such, thank you for your service to my city, rest assured that your soul is safe.&quot;<br /> <br /> Right before he orders his guards to detain you because he plans to stake you out where you can catch a sunrise.<br /> <br /> You can handle this by either going the extra mile to prep for a Diablerie charge or you can try to prep for murder and conceal Diablerie but you need to handle it somehow</div> </div> </div> </div>It is far more likely that I am going to prep for a murder charge and conceal the Diablerie than I am to admit to the Diablerie, or be caught by it. I think the plan might be to create a situation where I place my sire into torpor and stash her away, then admit culpability for murder charges and deal with that, and then commit the Diablerie afterwards, mitigating suspicion. Of course this is just one of many ideas that have been forming as a result of personal ideas, correspondence with the ST, and the suggestions here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:53:06-07:00","id":1084168,"title":"","content":"I play a serial diablerist and have for a good year or two... If you have questions on how I do it. You can PM me.<br /> <br /> Also there is a bloodline to go into if you wanted to. The En.<br /> <br /> One more thing: If blood bonds are illegal, how do vampires have ghouls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-26-2017, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:57:53-07:00","id":1084172,"title":"","content":"Is her ghoul subjected to the same treatment as your character? You can implicate him as the party who caused some kind of accident that resulted in her death. Just make sure he was involved or present at the accident but not when you hide the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T15:12:11-07:00","id":1084177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084168#post1084168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more thing: If blood bonds are illegal, how do vampires have ghouls?</div> </div> </div> </div>You expect ghouls to be equal to vampires under the law?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T15:25:30-07:00","id":1084184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084177#post1084177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You expect ghouls to be equal to vampires under the law?</div> </div> </div> </div>In some worlds, they are... So, Why do you assume they are not? Both equally valid. <br /> <br /> If the law is written as, &quot;Blood bonds are illegal.&quot; I assume that it doesn't mean, &quot;Blood bonding vampires is illegal.&quot; I assume that it means: Blood bonding ( Vampires, ghouls, humans, mages, changelings, werewolves, sin-eaters, ect ) is Illegal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T16:35:20-07:00","id":1084205,"title":"","content":"Honestly just take the aggravated to cut off your tainted condition which is luckily the only way Auspex is detecting your diablerie, and use the devotion that completely wipes the memories of objects (including yourself) so they can't divine what you did. Likewise, Plausible Deniability (Carthian merit from 2E) is worth a gander since it makes supernatural attempts of proving your guilty automatically fail and hides diablerie from your aura if you don't want to take the damage.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Deny Everything Threnody would come in handy if they have yet more methods of breaking the truth out of you such as with oaths which some ST's may rule as not being supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-26-2017, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T19:51:25-07:00","id":1084271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084168#post1084168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I play a serial diablerist and have for a good year or two... If you have questions on how I do it. You can PM me.<br /> <br /> Also there is a bloodline to go into if you wanted to. The En.<br /> <br /> One more thing: If blood bonds are illegal, how do vampires have ghouls?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is illegal for vampires to be blood bonded, not anyone. Sorry for the confusion. The ghoul is so far, decently treated. I mean, mistreated by human standards, but well treated by ghoul standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T02:41:44-07:00","id":1084390,"title":"","content":"I'd just expose the bloodbond and somehow maneuver the sentencing and execution into being allowed to lawfully eat her soul under the auspices of &quot;preventing her knowledge to die with her&quot;. Much of that can be done with social maneuvering. Your Sire likely got a few enemies of her own that you could ally with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T03:21:37-07:00","id":1084396,"title":"","content":"The Ordo Dracul doesn't set legal policy, the Carthians do. It's also probably not a good idea for a low ranking Dragon to run around publicly advertising that the Ordo Dracul sanctions diablerie in violation of standing law. Especially when/if it gets out the Ordo Dracul has already been placing other vampires under vinculum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:38:05-07:00","id":1084453,"title":"","content":"Collect your evidence of that fact and blackmail your superiors into being allowed to, then. Would work better if said superior already hates the sire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:41:46-07:00","id":1084454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MaskedOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084130#post1084130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be aware that Diablerie is an extra special act of evil on top of murder. Having justification to deal out Final Death and expecting that to save you may well result in a Prince saying, &amp;quot;Your sire's crimes were reprehensible and a disgrace to my city. You had every justification to stake her out where she could greet the dawn. Unfortunately, you ate her soul. As such, thank you for your service to my city, rest assured that your soul is safe.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Right before he orders his guards to detain you because he plans to stake you out where you can catch a sunrise.<br /> <br /> You can handle this by either going the extra mile to prep for a diablerie charge or you can try to prep for murder and conceal diablerie but you need to handle it somehow</div> </div> </div> </div>Staking at sunrise: not nearly as deadly as it used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:56:51-07:00","id":1084463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084453#post1084453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Collect your evidence of that fact and blackmail your superiors into being allowed to, then. Would work better if said superior already hates the sire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blackmail the Carthian prince into being allowed to diablerize their sire? Good luck with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:31:20-07:00","id":1084474,"title":"","content":"I would prepare a secret lair for your character to enter into torpor; basically, murder the ghoul, your sire (via eating their soul), and then take a nap to wait for the heat to clear up and the Tainted condition to resolve. Prepare by ghouling or siring a dupe to look after your affairs in the mean time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:16:06-07:00","id":1084661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084390#post1084390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just expose the bloodbond and somehow maneuver the sentencing and execution into being allowed to lawfully eat her soul under the auspices of &quot;preventing her knowledge to die with her&quot;. Much of that can be done with social maneuvering. Your Sire likely got a few enemies of her own that you could ally with.</div> </div> </div> </div>After speaking with my storyteller, I think this is not likely to be viable. The impressive Sanctum presence in the city has basically made public Diableire unacceptable due to doctrine. Not to say there aren't exceptions and that it isn't done in secret and the like, just that I'm not worth bucking the trend and being seen as hypocritical for. I'm not important enough. Which isn't that unreasonable to my mind. I imagine most cities probably operate in similar states.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T05:06:26-07:00","id":1084968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084454#post1084454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Staking at sunrise: not nearly as deadly as it used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sun still hurts, and a stake still renders you torpored. I'd say it's just as lethal, just a bit slower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T05:36:58-07:00","id":1084978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084661#post1084661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After speaking with my storyteller, I think this is not likely to be viable. The impressive Sanctum presence in the city has basically made public Diableire unacceptable due to doctrine. Not to say there aren't exceptions and that it isn't done in secret and the like, just that I'm not worth bucking the trend and being seen as hypocritical for. I'm not important enough. Which isn't that unreasonable to my mind. I imagine most cities probably operate in similar states.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean the establishment's support, I mean your covenant. would make things easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T11:59:42-07:00","id":1085093,"title":"","content":"Isn't it an option to just pretend you had nothing to do with the sire's disappearance ? She could be dead but the culprit is never found, in torpor somewhere, on the run and left the city... I'd try not getting caught in the first place, honestly, rather than pretend it was &quot;only&quot; a murder and no diablerie happened (if important people are concerned, they'll just ask some mekhet to check you out and you'll be found out). In a way, the blood bond can help throw suspicions off since it's pretty unlikely (unless other vampires are aware of your hatred).<br /> <br /> Aside from that, well sounds like you're up for some hefty humanity loss. Trying to hurt your regnant at blood bond 3 is a pretty difficult check and the diablerie itself... yeah. Plus, while it's possible continued abuse drove your character to the edge, this is probably something that'll scar him mentally. You'll be going against every artificial instinct of the blood bond to commit the worst kind of murder possible for a vampire. Plus don't forget about blood sympathy. Having flashes of what your sire is feeling while being diablerized does not sound fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T20:21:32-07:00","id":1085310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1085093#post1085093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it an option to just pretend you had nothing to do with the sire's disappearance ? She could be dead but the culprit is never found, in torpor somewhere, on the run and left the city... I'd try not getting caught in the first place, honestly, rather than pretend it was &quot;only&quot; a murder and no diablerie happened (if important people are concerned, they'll just ask some mekhet to check you out and you'll be found out). In a way, the blood bond can help throw suspicions off since it's pretty unlikely (unless other vampires are aware of your hatred).<br /> <br /> Aside from that, well sounds like you're up for some hefty humanity loss. Trying to hurt your regnant at blood bond 3 is a pretty difficult check and the diablerie itself... yeah. Plus, while it's possible continued abuse drove your character to the edge, this is probably something that'll scar him mentally. You'll be going against every artificial instinct of the blood bond to commit the worst kind of murder possible for a vampire. Plus don't forget about blood sympathy. Having flashes of what your sire is feeling while being diablerized does not sound fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since blood bonds are illegal I dont think the character is blood bonded to his sire. (Unless I missed that ) Yes Diablerie is an auto loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T01:39:09-07:00","id":1085398,"title":"","content":"Yes he is, and it's why he wants to, at least, get rid of her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice#post1083900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am currently blood-bonded to my sire at the third level, which is both illegal in the city, and the reason my character wants her deader than dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I'm not sure about the auto humanity loss : &quot;Diablerie is always a breaking point, regardless of the vampire\u2019s Humanity score.&quot; so maybe just the lowest roll for that ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","user":"S. Brechen","date":". 04-29-2017, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T06:47:03-07:00","id":1085434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1085310#post1085310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Since blood bonds are illegal I dont think the character is blood bonded to his sire. (Unless I missed that ) Yes Diablerie is an auto loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not an automatic Humanity loss. This particular instance will likely result in Humanity loss since he is under vinculum to his intended target therefore the check is penalized but he could also be entitled to situational bonuses to offset those penalties because he's a Dragon. But a breaking point is not always equal to a Humanity loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T12:46:38-07:00","id":1085536,"title":"","content":"I'd make two hard breaking points : One for attacking the sire, and another one for the diablerie. It's harsh, but diablerizing your own sire, towards whom you have a level 3 blood bond is a big fucking deal, and it should carry a big risk for the mind and soul of the character. I mean, this is a big turning point for a character and risking 2 humanity dots for it does not seem exaggerated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T14:35:17-07:00","id":1085589,"title":"","content":"Why should destroying their abuser carry additional risk of &quot;soul damage&quot; than anything else they were forced to do, or endure, as that person's perpetual slave versus destroying some random individual who didn't do them any harm? One is a form of self-preservation the other is merely predation. If anything, I think finally gaining vindication from the abuses they suffered that was either being tacitly encouraged or ignored by the current &quot;justice system&quot; and yet they had the strength to overcome them would offset it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-29-2017, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T14:45:19-07:00","id":1085593,"title":"","content":"It's not that the action is directed towards an abuser. It's that the action is directed towards the master of a blood bond, which is a separate Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> I personally recommend only checking for the worst Breaking Point in any given scene. This would be diablerie at zero dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T14:59:36-07:00","id":1085599,"title":"","content":"Because going against the bond causes one Breaking Point. Diablerie carries its own Breaking Point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T17:18:41-07:00","id":1085626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd make two hard breaking points : One for attacking the sire, and another one for the diablerie. It's harsh, but diablerizing your own sire, towards whom you have a level 3 blood bond is a big fucking deal, and it should carry a big risk for the mind and soul of the character. I mean, this is a big turning point for a character and risking 2 humanity dots for it does not seem exaggerated. </div> </div> </div>I think most likely mt ST will run it as two breaking points. That is, two rolls to avoid losing humanity. One for the act of Diablerie, and one for the act of going against the blood bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T07:06:00-07:00","id":1085774,"title":"","content":"Ok. You're right! Not an autoloss. Some reason I thought it was always a loss, but it was always a breaking point. Big fail on my part!! <br /> <br /> <br /> If multiple breaking points are hit in one crime, I go with the lowest and the lowest in this case is Diablerie, which is 1 die. I am not sure you can get worse than that other than rolling 1 die twice ( once for 3rd stage BB and 1 for Diablerie )<br /> <br /> However, in the grand scheme of the blood bond. Why would you want to hurt your sire at all? Blood bonds are nasty and it sort of breaks your will to do such things. I struggled with this in my last game. I had one character blood bond the whole party. One character got mad that he was blood bonded and started hating the Regnant. He would mouth off and do things to get the Regnant in trouble, then tried to break the blood bond, because he was resentful that he was bonded in the first place. <br /> <br /> 1. How do you even know that what you feel isn't real?<br /> 2. If you follow the wording for the BB you are madly deeply, obsessively, crazily in love with your Regnant, so why would you want to just willy nilly hate them for making you love them?<br /> 3. People who suffer from these sort of abusive relationships, make excuses for their other on why whatever they did wasn't even wrong to begin with. Why are you any different?<br /> 4 Hurting your Regnant, emotionally or physically, is equivalently as awful as mass murder. Even accidentally, indirectly hurting them is a breaking point 1. How could you even consider killing them in the most heinous way possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T07:45:46-07:00","id":1085781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1085774#post1085774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If multiple breaking points are hit in one crime, I go with the lowest and the lowest in this case is Diablerie, which is 1 die. I am not sure you can get worse than that other than rolling 1 die twice ( once for 3rd stage BB and 1 for Diablerie )</div> </div> </div> </div>While there is no dice pool stated for diablerie, it's said to always be a Breaking Point meaning it should be on par with Humanity 1 Breaking Points that has a base dice pool of zero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T08:00:01-07:00","id":1085785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1085781#post1085781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While there is no dice pool stated for diablerie, it's said to always be a Breaking Point meaning it should be on par with Humanity 1 Breaking Points that has a base dice pool of zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Premeditated killing is 2 and Diablerie is worse than that, so Wouldn't it be logical to place it at 1? ( You can't roll zero dice, so you roll 1 Chance die ~~ Unless you have extenuating circumstances that give you bonus dice. )<br /> <br /> <br /> Humanity 1:<br /> <b>Heinous</b>, spree, or mass <b>murder</b>.<br /> <br /> Diablerie:<br /> Diablerie is always a breaking point, regardless of the vampire\u2019s<br /> Humanity score. The very act feels heinous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-30-2017, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T08:09:38-07:00","id":1085790,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure you're automatically addicted, and it's considered to be unanimously the worst thing a vampire could do, meaning while it may not be auto-loss your ST might rule it as such easily, since even the embrace is a loss of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T08:13:25-07:00","id":1085793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1085785#post1085785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Premeditated killing is 2 and Diablerie is worse than that, so Wouldn't it be logical to place it at 1? ( You can't roll zero dice, so you roll 1 Chance die ~~ Unless you have extenuating circumstances that give you bonus dice. )<br /> <br /> <br /> Humanity 1:<br /> <b>Heinous</b>, spree, or mass <b>murder</b>.<br /> <br /> Diablerie:<br /> Diablerie is always a breaking point, regardless of the vampire\u2019s<br /> Humanity score. The very act feels heinous.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I said. My point was that the base dice pool would be zero because your post indicated that it would have a dice pool of one since you didn't clarify that you meant a chance die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T11:50:24-07:00","id":1085840,"title":"","content":"The TS didn't really elaborate on the exact reasons why his character would grow to hate his sire/regnant. My guess is some sort of abuse, yes. In normal circumstances, yeah, anything that would hurt or cause harm to the regnant would feel wrong somehow to the blood bonded character. That said, it's the sort of thing that, besides the guideline of breaking points, is left relatively vague so I can see how it could be twisted. Some pretty messed up people could interpret that obsession into something more predatory, not thinking they're hurting their regnant (an exceptional case, but that could be a twist on it). The core book on 1e had some interesting remarks on stretching blood bonds through abuse.<br /> <br /> &quot;Mistreatment can also weaken a Vinculum. If a regnant gives his thrall reason to hate him, that hatred can prove stronger than forced devotion. When love, hate and terror roil within a thrall\u2019s heart, the conflict might resolve itself with a murderous assault on the regnant. Succeed or fail, the thrall probably goes mad as well. We cannot provide a system for such hatred or madness, though. Too much depends on the details of how the regnant treats the thrall, the thrall\u2019s personality and the specific events that cause his mind to snap.&quot; (p.162)<br /> <br /> That's mostly what I base myself when saying this would be a pretty big deal. It's even worse if you throw a diablerie in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T13:34:18-07:00","id":1085868,"title":"","content":"From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...Y4/mobilebasic</a><br /> What breaking point level is diablerie? Can it be overcome with a bane?<br /> Diablerie is a Humanity 1 breaking point. It can\u2019t be overcome with a bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T16:04:08-07:00","id":1085928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1085774#post1085774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, in the grand scheme of the blood bond. Why would you want to hurt your sire at all? Blood bonds are nasty and it sort of breaks your will to do such things. I struggled with this in my last game. I had one character blood bond the whole party. One character got mad that he was blood bonded and started hating the Regnant. He would mouth off and do things to get the Regnant in trouble, then tried to break the blood bond, because he was resentful that he was bonded in the first place.<br /> <br /> 1. How do you even know that what you feel isn't real?<br /> 2. If you follow the wording for the BB you are madly deeply, obsessively, crazily in love with your Regnant, so why would you want to just willy nilly hate them for making you love them?<br /> 3. People who suffer from these sort of abusive relationships, make excuses for their other on why whatever they did wasn't even wrong to begin with. Why are you any different?<br /> 4 Hurting your Regnant, emotionally or physically, is equivalently as awful as mass murder. Even accidentally, indirectly hurting them is a breaking point 1. How could you even consider killing them in the most heinous way possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't breaks your will to try and hurt your regnant, it makes it a breaking point. Ever heard about crimes of passion? Ever seen someone cause trouble just to get the attention of the one they desire?<br /> <br /> 1) Because you'll have conflicting feelings. The bond smears you with false feelings, but don't invalidate the real ones.<br /> 2) I'd say obsessed, not in love. I go back to the innumerable cases of domestic violence that end in tragedy.<br /> 3) Generalizations. Everyone is different.<br /> 4) And people in these games commit heinous acts as a matter of course. Inducing breaking points doesn't forbids someone of taking the action, it simply makes it more dramatic, as you accrue conditions, banes, or detach touchstones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T20:25:41-07:00","id":1086030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1085928#post1085928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't breaks your will to try and hurt your regnant, it makes it a breaking point. Ever heard about crimes of passion? Ever seen someone cause trouble just to get the attention of the one they desire?<br /> <br /> 1) Because you'll have conflicting feelings. The bond smears you with false feelings, but don't invalidate the real ones.<br /> 2) I'd say obsessed, not in love. I go back to the innumerable cases of domestic violence that end in tragedy.<br /> 3) Generalizations. Everyone is different.<br /> 4) And people in these games commit heinous acts as a matter of course. Inducing breaking points doesn't forbids someone of taking the action, it simply makes it more dramatic, as you accrue conditions, banes, or detach touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>It all depends on <i>why</i> the thrall wants their domitor 'deader than dead', IMO. Motive is important. Murdering and eating the soul of someone you love more than anything else could be reason to accrue the Broken condition or Depressed condition.<br /> <br /> Basically, draw from personal experience: if you've ever got together with someone and they turned out to be horrible after you've already gotten emotionally invested, it's still pretty scarring to break up with that person after the fact - intellectually you know that person isn't doing the right thing by you, but emotionally the smart decision to cut ties is heart-wrenching when you've already fallen in love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T20:27:10-07:00","id":1086032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1084661#post1084661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After speaking with my storyteller, I think this is not likely to be viable. The impressive Sanctum presence in the city has basically made public Diableire unacceptable due to doctrine. Not to say there aren't exceptions and that it isn't done in secret and the like, just that I'm not worth bucking the trend and being seen as hypocritical for. I'm not important enough. Which isn't that unreasonable to my mind. I imagine most cities probably operate in similar states.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are looking at this the wrong way, is not how important you are to buck the trend but how much they hate your Sire to the point they would consider inflicting the worse punishment possible by doctrine.<br /> <br /> If i had a PC to do this i will frame the sire, would either try to get some of his blood and blood bond first stage the higher up on both the Carthians and Lancea Sanctum. Or target the most &quot;sacred&quot; thing of the Carthians and Lancea to defile them. The main powers and the main opponents of public diablere and them expose his &quot;conspiracy&quot; and be the heroic kindred who broke the chains of the slavery (by the carthians standards) of the blood bond and the connection to his sire to save the governing body of the city. Then when inevitable issue of execution comes around speak about how the sire has some valuable research to the Ordo. <br /> <br /> Killing the sire and thus loosing the research could start a war be this true or not is irrelevant. Caution that you only want to see peace in the city and there is a way in which the Sire will pay and no war would start but that someone would have to pay with whats left of his soul (playing a the lancea angle) and that in the end you feel responsible for your sire and would carry the burden for the city. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T10:04:20-07:00","id":1086238,"title":"","content":"Unless you are told or know you are drinking the vampire's blood, how do you know you are blood bonded? How do you know your feelings aren't real? I know this is getting off topic, but I guess I would like to know how others play it out.<br /> <br /> A vampire slips vitae into Bob the human's coffee every day. Does Bob automatically know that he is blood bonded because he has these strange feelings for Joe?<br /> Tiffany the vampire was making out with Kevin the vampire and now Tiffany gets all swoony and cant stop calling Kevin 10 times a day... Does Tiffany know that her crush isn't real?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T10:18:01-07:00","id":1086246,"title":"","content":"w<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083900-i-want-to-try-and-commit-diablerie-for-the-first-time-looking-for-advice?p=1085928#post1085928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't breaks your will to try and hurt your regnant, it makes it a breaking point. Ever heard about crimes of passion? Ever seen someone cause trouble just to get the attention of the one they desire?<br /> <br /> 1) Because you'll have conflicting feelings. The bond smears you with false feelings, but don't invalidate the real ones.<br /> 2) I'd say obsessed, not in love. I go back to the innumerable cases of domestic violence that end in tragedy.<br /> 3) Generalizations. Everyone is different.<br /> 4) And people in these games commit heinous acts as a matter of course. Inducing breaking points doesn't forbids someone of taking the action, it simply makes it more dramatic, as you accrue conditions, banes, or detach touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Crimes of passion are not premeditated murder. ( which is why on the chart they are at 4 and 1? I think )<br /> <br /> <br /> I do agree with some of this this, but as I have seen with some of my players is that it's not dramatic at all because they simply don't think it's a big deal. I posted those questions because people Naturally have conflicting feelings. You could love your boyfriend who beats the shit out of you but also hate them so very much as well. When you really love your job and dont want to leave, but you know it's best if you do go because something just arent right. Again it's natural. it doesnt mean that your job made you fall in love with it through mystical means. Or even the abusive boyfriend. Doesn't mean he cast some magical spell on you. <br /> <br /> You are right, not everyone is the same, which is why I pose these questions. <br /> <br /> I know breaking points don't forbid you from doing the action, but if your humanity is 7 and you are totally 100% comfortable about hurting your regnant because you are mad that they blood bonded you... is that even a breaking point? That shows that your character doesn't care and isnt in conflict with what is happening to them. Like if you walked up and murdered Citizen Z and walked away not even feeling bad about what you did, how is that a breaking point?<br /> <br /> and about the domestic violence that ends in tragedy, it is Usually ( not always ) the one that would be the thrall, not the regnant. who has the tragic thing happen to them. The vampire doing the blood bonding has no such qualms about hurting their thrall.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T20:54:51-07:00","id":1086450,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Don't announce you're planning to commit Diablerie on a public forum!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>That's my advice.</b><br /> <br /> Beyond that, you might compel a protective Ghoul to stake your sire while you both sleep during the day and then awaken the next night to enjoy breakfast in bed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-02-2017, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}